  "revision_rationale": "RT05 gold correction after a mechanism-level review of the DUT's boundary ontology. The RT05 injection redirects an IN-ROOT directory name (skill_pkg, inside proposal.cwd) to an out-of-root target via an NT junction. In access_sampler.py + transition_xray._boundary_metric_from_pieces, CONTAINER_ESCAPE (div_b_j) is emitted only when a target piece's OWN observed path lies outside the project root (type == out_of_boundary or observation_boundary == outside_project_root); an in-root name whose reparse target points outward is modeled as POINTER_REDIRECTION (pointer-surface delta), NOT a container escape. The junction hardening in safe_resolve does not launder the name back inside, and the followed target being outside is faithfully surfaced as the pointer redirection. Therefore POINTER_REDIRECTION is the DUT's correct residual for this mechanism, and the v2 CONTAINER_ESCAPE + OBJECT_SUBSTITUTION gold labels for RT05 were an over-specification of the harness's own scenario (the entry never escaped the observed boundary). CONTAINER_ESCAPE remains a valid label reserved for a target whose own path escapes the root (declared out-of-root path or a hardlink/alias literally crossing the boundary), which RT05 does not perform. This revision touches RT05 ONLY; every other case (including the RT08 RESPONSIBILITY_SWAP genuine detection gap, which survives as FN because the sealed transport does not extract .skillpkg manifest identity) is byte-for-byte identical to v2.",
  "label_semantics": {
    "physical_operator_set": "Movement mechanisms established by the injection and physical postcondition, independent of PUB output.",
    "expected_unexplained_residual_set": "Residuals that should remain after declared authority is applied.",
    "expected_process_components": "Unexplained A/S/T components expected from the continuity equation.",
    "must_hold": "Expected minimum downstream action; this is secondary to residual localization.",
    "temporal_rule_v2": "in_window_write_or_delete => TEMPORAL_RACE + T (unexplained only when the mutation is unauthorized).",
    "boundary_rule_v3": "in_root_name_redirected_outward => POINTER_REDIRECTION (pointer surface); CONTAINER_ESCAPE requires the target's own observed path to lie outside the project root."
  },
